   "source": [
    "# 🧪 Exercise 1: Create a temperature converter tool\n",
    "\n",
    "@tool\n",
    "def celsius_to_fahrenheit(celsius: float) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        celsius: Temperature in Celsius\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        Temperature in Fahrenheit\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    fahrenheit = (celsius * 9/5) + 32\n",
    "    return f\"{celsius}°C = {fahrenheit:.1f}°F\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test it\n",
    "print(\"Testing converter:\", celsius_to_fahrenheit.invoke(25))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ❓ FAQ\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q: What's the difference between an agent and a bot?**\n",
    "A: An agent uses LLMs + tools + loops. Bots are more general automation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q: Can agents run forever?**\n",
    "A: Yes, if there's no termination condition! Always set max iterations.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q: Do agents always need tools?**\n",
    "A: Technically no, but tools are what make them useful.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q: How many loops can an agent take?**\n",
    "A: Depends on task complexity. Simple tasks: 1-3. Complex: 10+."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ✅ Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "You learned:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Agents** = LLM + Loop + Tools + Memory\n",
    "2. **Agent loop** = Observe → Reason → Act → Repeat\n",
    "3. **Agents vs LLMs**: Agents iterate, use tools, maintain state\n",
    "4. **When to use agents**: Multi-step tasks requiring tool use\n",
